            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Punjabi for black, then the Punjabi for white."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ਭੂਰਾ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਭੂਰਾ — bhūrā — \"brown\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਭੂਰਾ (bhūrā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from bhrūra, \"brown\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants (CDIAL 9690). CDIAL compares Indo-European bhrū-no-, which is behind English brown."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
