              "text": "ਸਵੇਰ (saver) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from savela, \"in time, early\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants (CDIAL 13291). It is built from sa-, \"with\", and velā, \"time\"; Punjabi saver means \"morning, dawn\"."
